{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BoNkVIsiQ7CAQjqw5",
	"notes": "An ordinary human drawn into the service of the Ruinous Powers: a hive-gang tough, a fanatic from a rotting agri-world, a cult congregant given a gun and a promise. Untrained and unaugmented, at about 42 points (physiology, traits and skills, no gear) he sits at the bottom of the framework's ladder, below the 100-175 trained-soldier tier; the framework's figure is roughly 40-80 and the build lands at the low end of it, since Cultist's Devotion's -20 and a slow mind (IQ 9, -20) eat most of what the faith's small gifts (High Pain Threshold, Fearlessness, Single-Minded) and a poor spread of skills buy. Equipment is in the wargear files, not here: autogun or autopistol, a crude blade, a flak vest or rags. Raise skills and add a single god's Mark (Chaos Traits) for a cult champion.",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tOxdGCJfxW-siAPNv",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An ordinary adult human, malnourished more often than not.\n\nDesign: ST 10, the human baseline (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "tjF_0hiK6Ypkn9wLU",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: No training beyond a few shots at the range or a few brawls in the cult's cellars.\n\nDesign: DX 10, baseline.",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "taV45Jq0JUWKodS-F",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Cultists are taken from the desperate and the credulous, and the cult does the thinking.\n\nDesign: IQ 9, Decreased IQ -1 (B16, 20/level) = -20 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": -20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "iq",
					"amount": -1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tKwfwltPGTBGzYC8Y",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Ordinary health.\n\nDesign: HT 10, baseline.",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 0
		},
		{
			"id": "t255sBFEquLbQmIBT",
			"name": "Fit",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Years of hard labour and cult-cellar brawling keep a cultist wiry.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fit (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tycGtRvBkBIPJK1ud",
			"name": "Single-Minded",
			"reference": "B85",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A fanatic's one-track zeal; the Black Library cultist fights through terror and pain towards the altar.\n\nDesign: Single-Minded (B85), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Chaos"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tT65fQ2dl_g5sRuYy",
			"name": "Fearlessness",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Drugs and doctrine have burned out most of a cultist's fear.\n\nDesign: Fearlessness 2 (B55, 2/level), 4 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Chaos"
			],
			"points_per_level": 2,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "tWr4ElrVKCrXhlQDS",
			"name": "High Pain Threshold",
			"reference": "B59",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Cult fanatics are shown in Black Library's Inquisition fiction enduring wounds and drugs that would put a sane man down, driven by faith and stimulants.\n\nDesign: High Pain Threshold (B59), 10 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Chaos"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "TIu-ptbxc1Fx4vmeB",
			"name": "Cultist's Devotion",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Chaos cults draw ordinary men and women into the service of the Ruinous Powers. Black Library's Inquisition fiction and Codex background treat the typical cultist as a fanatic indifferent to anyone outside the cult, and the same cultist as the first to die for a Dark God.\n\nDesign: Fanaticism (B136) -15 and Callous (B125) -5, self-control 12 = -20 points. A cultist who follows a single god's Mark also takes that Mark's own disadvantages; Undivided cultists take this in place of Mark of Chaos Undivided.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Chaos",
				"Chaos Cultist"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tKZdn9LAH99-eevfs",
					"name": "Fanaticism (Chaos)",
					"reference": "B136",
					"local_notes": "Devoted to the Ruinous Powers; takes risks for the cult and cannot be reasoned out of it.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental"
					],
					"base_points": -15
				},
				{
					"id": "tisi1aEMRXhWAqX-q",
					"name": "Callous",
					"reference": "B125",
					"local_notes": "Indifferent to the suffering of anyone outside the cult.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental"
					],
					"base_points": -5
				}
			]
		}
	],
