		{
			"id": "eOmkIGeyAP66g7hrL",
			"description": "Autopistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A cheap, mass-produced sidearm found across a billion hive worlds: gang muscle, PDF conscripts and Guard officers who don't rate a laspistol all carry one. Consistently portrayed in Guard and Arbites fiction as the low-status \"poor man's laspistol.\"\n\nDesign: No framework anchor covers stub weapons directly, but they must stay proportional to the autogun anchor (7d pi) they're built alongside. The autopistol is the cheapest, lightest pistol-calibre round in the file: 3d+1 pi (avg 11.5), about 47% of the autogun's average of 24.5, full pi wounding for a modern jacketed round. It sits below the stub automatic (3d+2) and the stub revolver (4d), the ordering FFG-line background gives for relative calibration. Against flak (DR 30) it penetrates 0% of hits, so it is relevant only against unarmoured targets; a GM wanting it to matter against flak would need to depart from this pistol-family scaling, which this entry does not do on its own authority. The Manstopper usage keeps the pi+/divisor (0.5) shape with +1 damage over the ball round (3d+2(0.5) pi+, avg 12.5): it never penetrates flak or better (0% of hits, effective DR doubled by the divisor) but hits unarmoured flesh harder, the standard GURPS way to model an expanding round: more damage to flesh, worse against any DR. Handling: weight (2 lb) and min ST (7) follow GURPS's pistol-weight convention (roughly ST 7 for a service-calibre autoloader this size) rather than the shoulder-arm sqrt formula, which this project reserves for rifles and heavier weapons. Bulk -2 and Rcl 2 are ordinary pistol figures.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"tech_level": "7",
			"legality_class": "4",
			"base_value": "80",
